Empty the GamePak prefetch buffer on every PC write, in the interpreter and
in generated code.

The GBA profile models the GamePak prefetch buffer after mGBA's
GBAMemoryStall (Bus::prefetch_stall; the runtime keeps the buffer's
position in RuntimeWaitTable::last_prefetched_pc). mGBA forgets that
position on every PC write: ARMWritePC calls setActiveRegion, and
GBASetActiveRegion sets lastPrefetchedPc = 0 (mGBA 0.10.5,
src/gba/memory.c:273; the same in 1d201b22, the timing model's reference).
Nothing reset it here, so a loop that runs from the cartridge and stores to
RAM kept, across its branch back, the position of the opcodes fetched after
the loop: the buffer looked nearly full, the store let it fetch one
halfword instead of five, and the store cost 8 cycles instead of mGBA's 4.
With WAITCNT 0x4317, `cmp r1, r2; strcc r3, [r1], #4; bcc` costs 26 cycles
per iteration instead of 22.

The change:

- Bus::prefetch_reset() (bus.h): a PC write empties the buffer. A no-op by
  default, as a bus without a prefetch buffer has nothing to empty.
- Interpreter::step calls it after any instruction that wrote R15 (taken
  branches, data-processing and load writes to R15, LDM with PC, exception
  returns), after the instruction's own stalls, which come before the
  write. The refill's fetch waits do not read the position.
- The codegen clears g_runtime_waits.last_prefetched_pc after the refill of
  every direct branch (emit_direct_branch), whatever the target region, on
  every path that leaves through it (loop back-edge, tail transfer, call).
  PC writes known only at run time charge runtime_refill_cycles, which the
  runtime resets.

SWI and IRQ entry do not go through Interpreter::step; the runtime that
enters them decides (the position matters only while the CPU runs from the
cartridge, and both exceptions return there through a PC write that resets
it).

This is half of the fix; the runtime's half overrides prefetch_reset in its
buses and resets the position in runtime_refill_cycles (gbarecomp:
0011-prefetch-reset-on-pc-write.patch in the same repository as this
patch). Without it, this patch builds but the interpreter keeps the old
behavior while generated static branches reset, so the two backends no
longer charge ROM loops alike.

Tested on macOS arm64 (Apple clang 21) at arm-recomp-core 1f13cdf, inside
gbarecomp 5e89943 with its runtime half:

- gbarecomp's ctest, 52 of 52 (with the gba-tests test ROMs). codegen_tests
  compares, for every instruction of its corpus relocated into the
  cartridge under five WAITCNT/EWRAM settings (one with the buffer's
  position seeded just ahead of the instruction), the interpreter's and the
  generated code's cycles and buffer position. A new interpreter_smoke case
  checks that prefetch_reset runs once after each kind of PC write and
  never otherwise (mov, cmp, str, a branch not taken).
- Mutations: without the interpreter's call, interpreter_smoke fails on
  every PC write; without the codegen's reset, codegen_tests fails on
  arm_b_forward, arm_bl, arm_b_backward and thumb_beq_taken; without the
  runtime_refill_cycles reset, on arm_pop_r4_pc, arm_ldmia_pc_computed,
  arm_ldmia_empty_wb and thumb_pop_r4_pc.
- A synthetic 4 KiB ROM (no Nintendo data, header logo zero), prefetch1,
  times three loops of 64 stores to EWRAM from the cartridge with WAITCNT
  0x4317, each between two timer 0 reads at F/1: the loop above, the same
  loop closed by `bxcc r6` (a PC write known only at run time), and a THUMB
  loop (str, adds, cmp, bcc). mGBA 0.10.5 measures 1424, 1424 and 892
  cycles. gbarecomp 5e89943 measures 1673, 1673 and 1141 on generated code
  (GBARECOMP_STRICT_STATIC=1, fully static) and on the interpreter
  (GBARECOMP_FORCE_INTERP=1, BIOS interpreted too); with this patch and its
  runtime half, 1424, 1424 and 892 on both. The generator and config are in
  tests/repro/ of https://github.com/nvergez/moto-racer-advanced-browser
  (make_rom.py, prefetch1.toml); attach them when filing this patch.
- A commercial game whose race start-up clears 54,459 words of EWRAM with
  the loop above, from the cartridge, before it copies its race code to
  IWRAM: without the fix the race code arrives one frame later than in
  mGBA (the clear costs 217,829 cycles more, 0.78 frame), and every later
  input lands one game frame off. With both halves (and the IRQ entry
  cycles of 0012 in the runtime), the clear's instruction timeline equals
  mGBA's to the cycle, the race code arrives on mGBA's frame, and the race
  plays as in mGBA (same lap times, same RAM on every race frame but three
  of the loading screen).

diff --git a/profiles/armv4t_gba/arm_codegen.cpp b/profiles/armv4t_gba/arm_codegen.cpp
index a6c4dba..2a8c401 100644
--- a/profiles/armv4t_gba/arm_codegen.cpp
+++ b/profiles/armv4t_gba/arm_codegen.cpp
@@ -461,6 +461,11 @@ std::string emit_direct_branch(uint32_t target, uint32_t branch_pc,
         const std::string refill = static_refill_expr(target, thumb_link);
         if (!refill.empty()) s << indent << cyc << " += " << refill << ";\n";
     }
+    // The PC write empties the GamePak prefetch buffer, as
+    // Bus::prefetch_reset does in the interpreter (mGBA
+    // GBASetActiveRegion). PC writes known only at run time charge
+    // runtime_refill_cycles, which resets it too.
+    s << indent << "g_runtime_waits.last_prefetched_pc = 0u;\n";
 
     if (!is_link &&
         target >= ctx.current_function_addr &&
diff --git a/profiles/armv4t_gba/bus.h b/profiles/armv4t_gba/bus.h
index 01172df..be70114 100644
--- a/profiles/armv4t_gba/bus.h
+++ b/profiles/armv4t_gba/bus.h
@@ -61,6 +61,15 @@ struct Bus {
                                    bool /*thumb*/) {
         return wait;
     }
+
+    // A PC write (any branch, a data-processing or load instruction that
+    // writes R15, an exception return) empties the GamePak prefetch
+    // buffer: the next stall starts from no prefetched opcodes. mGBA's
+    // GBASetActiveRegion, which ARMWritePC calls on every PC write, sets
+    // lastPrefetchedPc = 0. The interpreter calls this after any
+    // instruction that wrote R15; generated code resets the same state
+    // after every PC write it makes. The default has no prefetch buffer.
+    virtual void prefetch_reset() {}
 };
 
 }  // namespace armv4t
diff --git a/profiles/armv4t_gba/interpreter.cpp b/profiles/armv4t_gba/interpreter.cpp
index e11046e..6c1b030 100644
--- a/profiles/armv4t_gba/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/profiles/armv4t_gba/interpreter.cpp
@@ -1221,6 +1221,11 @@ Interpreter::Result Interpreter::step(CPUState& cpu, Bus& bus, const Instr& i,
         *cycles_out = c;
     }
 
+    // The PC write empties the GamePak prefetch buffer (Bus::prefetch_reset,
+    // mGBA GBASetActiveRegion). After the instruction's own stalls, which
+    // came before the write; the refill above reads only fetch waits.
+    if (wrote_pc) bus.prefetch_reset();
+
     if (exception_returned) {
         return Result::ExceptionReturn;
     }
